Texture parking acts on an iOS memory warning (Minato, patch 0022).

Why: parking reacted only to the available memory it reads at its ticks, and iOS warns before that number shows the
pressure (an app was ended 18 s after its first warning). ANGLEMetalMemoryWarning(), callable from any thread, sets a
deadline one second ahead (atomics only; the work stays on the app's GL thread): until it, each tick parks as in the
emergency band whatever the available memory says (textures idle for 33 ms, the in-memory packed copies of restored
textures go, the restores' staging is finished once). The park line appends " warn=<n>", the warnings seen.

